  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#set-and-filter-html:~:text=into%20target%2E-,Let,fragment%2E\n\nWhy do we have these steps? They make nodes non-inert if *contextElement*'s node document is non-inert. This can cause images to load, for example. (Gecko doesn't follow the spec and creates an inert `DocumentFragment` ([source](https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/source/dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp#6388-6402)).)\n\n*newChildren* is already an inert `Document`, that can be sanitized directly.\n\n@otherdaniel @mozfreddyb @evilpie ",
